one guy who didn't win  at least hasn't won so far in his nfl  career jadavian clowney this is the  prime example of the downside of the  rookie wage scale it was put in place to  ensure that busts don't suck millions  out of the system without earning it so  the guys who do earn it  don't get paid what they would have  gotten paid jd and clowney if he'd have  been the first overall pick four years  earlier than he was in 2014 he would  have gotten so much more money than he  received but he still hasn't gotten a  second contract and you've got the  texans playing games with him and not  that there's i look i  they have every right to do it  they are allowed to squat on him for the  five years of his rookie contract  they're allowed under the cba to  franchise tag him once or twice or even  three times if they want to and then he  becomes a free agent at some point down  the road when his value is far less than  what it would have been they're allowed  to do that the one thing that kind of  put me over the edge though the games  they're playing with the franchise tag  designation of judaevian clowney and now  a grievance rightfully has been filed  over whether or not he's defensive end  or a linebacker we're only talking about  a million and a half dollars and i know  that's a lot of money  in isolation but but still for a guy who  has been a loyal and faithful employee  of the franchise who hasn't been  clamoring for a new contract publicly  who hasn't held out hasn't even thought  about holding out when he was under  contract and currently he's not under  contract i i i don't know why you do  this to the guy and at some point you  have to wonder  what impact does it have on the locker  room somebody asked me that question  yesterday as it relates to clowney not  getting a long-term deal  and my reaction was well you know in the  eyes of the locker room i think it's  worse to have an undrafted guy like aj  bouier that puts in four years does all  the right things and has to go somewhere  else to get paid like he had to go to  jacksonville to get paid  with clowney the other guys in the  locker room say hey he was the first  overall pick in the draft he's made a  hell of a lot more money than us and i  don't think that there is as sensitive  to the niceties of how it used to be  when a guy would really get big money to  be the first overall pick  but when there's a perception you're  screwing around with the guy when you're  nickel and dimming him and again i know  a million and a half dollars is a lot of  money in isolation but when you're  talking about 190 million salary cap  when you're talking about a guy who has  been part of the team all these years  i just  i wonder at what point it it  it becomes  a factor  among the players and i wonder how much  hand-holding and sweet talking jack  easterby's gonna have to do in the  locker room if players are pissed off  about the way that they're handling  jadavian clowny it's a very simple  analysis you're either a linebacker or a  defensive end based upon where you lined  up for the majority of the snaps  during a given year now it gets  complicated because linebackers in a 3-4  often end up with a hand in the dirt  rushing the passer but you know we we  saw this with jimmy graham several years  ago graham lost that argument whether he  was a receiver versus a tight end we're  going to see it again now would you  davey and clowny we shouldn't have to  the texans should just do the right  thing and pay this guy as a defensive  end and move forward or better yet give  him a long-term contract the long-term  contract that he earned  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports
 

